<%#
    Who is logged in and taking the exam but was not found at any table. The
    names sit in a popup rather than on the page: it is a short list that
    matters a great deal for a moment, and a block of names standing open
    pushes the room down the page every time it changes length.

    While more than ten are still to place the count stands on its own, with
    no popup: at that stage it is just how far the mapping has got, and a list
    of names would be a work list rather than a warning.
%>
<% if unplaced.empty? %>
<span class="room-missing-none"><%= bootstrap_icon("check-circle") %> Everyone is accounted for.</span>

<% elsif names_hidden %>
<span class="room-missing-count"><strong><%= unplaced.size %></strong> still to place</span>

<% else %>
<details class="room-missing">
    <summary>
        <%= bootstrap_icon("exclamation-triangle") %>
        <strong><%= unplaced.size %></strong>
        <%= "student".pluralize(unplaced.size) %> not in the room
    </summary>

    <div class="room-missing-list">
        <p class="room-missing-header">
            Logged in and taking the exam, but not found at any table.
        </p>
        <% unplaced.each do |submit| %>
        <div class="room-missing-student">
            <%= link_to submit.user_name, submit, class: "text-decoration-none", data: { 'turbo-frame' => 'modal' } %>
            <small class="text-body-secondary"><%= submit.user&.pin %></small>
        </div>
        <% end %>
    </div>
</details>
<% end %>
